; Colliding events whose boxes lie 2^31 or more rows apart, each box within
; int's range. At 1920x1080 the 960x540 script scales by 2, so the second
; event's margin puts its box near INT_MIN, while the others sit in the
; frame. The difference of two tops then wraps in the comparison of the
; collision boxes, which is no longer transitive, so the order the sort gives
; them decides where the last event goes: pushed up above "moved down", it is
; left overlapping "moved up". The far event is clipped away: its position
; leaves int's range in 26.6 fixed point, and libass built for aarch64 then
; draws it inside the frame where libass built for armv7 draws nothing. At
; 1280x720 the scale is 4/3, nothing wraps, and the events stack by value.
